>> title: Seekh Kabab
>> category: Smoked & Grilled
>> tags: lamb, indian, minced, grill, starter
>> counters: Curry House
>> aka: seekh kebab, sheekh kabab, seekh kebabs, lamb seekh, shami's cousin
>> pairs-with: mint-chutney, kachumber, naan
>> servings: 6
>> time: 1 hr 45 min
>> step.1: knead 5 min, until it turns tacky and pulls at the bowl
>> step.2: chill 1 hr
>> step.3: press onto flat skewers in a long sleeve
>> step.4: grill 10 min, turning by the handle

Knead @ground lamb{2%lb}(900 g; 20% fat, ground twice), @yellow onion{1%medium}(grated and wrung dry in a cloth), @ginger-garlic paste{2%Tbs}(34 g), @green chiles{2}(chopped fine), @cilantro{1/4%cup}(chopped), @mint{2%Tbs}(chopped), @garam masala{2%tsp}, @roasted gram flour{2%Tbs}(20 g) and @kosher salt{2%tsp} in a #bowl{} ~knead{5%min}, pushing it against the side with the heel of your hand until it turns tacky and starts pulling back at you.

Chill @&(~1)kabab mixture{} ~chill{1%hr}. Cold fat and worked protein are the two things holding this on the skewer, and it will slide off the moment either is missing.

Press @&(~1)chilled mixture{} onto flat metal #skewers{} in a wet hand, working from the middle out into a sleeve as long as your palm and no thicker than a thumb, then rake it lengthways with your fingers.

Grill @&(~1)skewers{} over hard charcoal ~grill{10%min}, turning them by the handle every two minutes and basting with @melted ghee{2%Tbs}(28 g), until the ridges are dark and the fat is dropping.

Flat skewers, not round: a round one turns and the meat stays where it was. The wrung-out onion matters as much — grated onion carries a lot of water, and water is what makes a kabab collapse into the fire. Roasted gram flour is the binder a curry house uses and there is no egg in it. Off the skewer and into a naan with kachumber and mint chutney is the way these are actually eaten.
